Modern Sōtō Zen: Suzuki (@buddhist-zen-mind: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @buddhist-further-reading, #source @buddhist-source-zen-mind, #philosophy @buddhist-dogen, #buddhism @buddhist-dogen) { r_1XY4XRP870EMBAEAJQ39WGQ2XZ
**Read:** Read the complete collection of talks, attending to the setting of instruction and the account of sitting and cultivation. An accessible style can invite difficult questions rather than supplying a new ladder of slogans.

**Investigate:** Choose a statement that seems paradoxical or contrary to an earlier teaching. Explain its context, offer a careful interpretation, and identify what the comparison leaves unresolved. Do not assume that every use of practice or awakening has the same instructional function.

**Check:** identify the passages, edition, and interpretation another reader would need to examine your account. Let the comparison modify an earlier view when the evidence warrants it.

**Source:** [Zen Mind, Beginner’s Mind](../sources/Zen-mind.lingua#r_1M52EZP2JCJY8MCWHCJXFAN9WX).

